8: # Canvas System Specification
9: 
10: ## Overview
11: 
12: This specification defines the technical implementation requirements for the Canvas drawing system in CycoTui. The Canvas provides a flexible drawing surface with multiple grid types, coordinate transformation, and layer-based rendering capabilities.
13: 
14: ## Scope
15: 
16: This specification covers:
17: - Canvas widget implementation
18: - Grid type interfaces and implementations
19: - Coordinate system transformation
20: - Shape drawing interface
21: - Layer management system
22: - Text label overlay system
23: 
24: ## Requirements
25: 
26: ### Canvas Widget Interface
27: 
28: ```csharp
29: public class Canvas<TDrawFunction> : IWidget
30:     where TDrawFunction : class // Action<ICanvasContext> or similar
31: {
32:     // Configuration properties
33:     public Block? Block { get; set; }
34:     public double[] XBounds { get; set; } // [left, right]
35:     public double[] YBounds { get; set; } // [bottom, top]
36:     public Color BackgroundColor { get; set; }
37:     public Marker MarkerType { get; set; }
38:     
39:     // Fluent configuration methods
40:     public Canvas<TDrawFunction> WithBlock(Block block);
41:     public Canvas<TDrawFunction> WithXBounds(double left, double right);
42:     public Canvas<TDrawFunction> WithYBounds(double bottom, double top);
43:     public Canvas<TDrawFunction> WithBackgroundColor(Color color);
44:     public Canvas<TDrawFunction> WithMarker(Marker marker);
45:     public Canvas<TDrawFunction> Paint(TDrawFunction drawFunction);
46:     
47:     // Widget implementation
48:     public void Render(Rect area, IBuffer buffer);
49: }
50: ```
51: 
52: ### Grid Type Interface
53: 
54: ```csharp
55: public interface IGrid
56: {
57:     // Grid properties
58:     (double Width, double Height) Resolution { get; }
59:     
60:     // Grid operations
61:     void Paint(int x, int y, Color color);
62:     ILayer Save();
63:     void Reset();
64: }
65: 
66: public interface ILayer
67: {
68:     string Content { get; }
69:     IReadOnlyList<(Color Foreground, Color Background)> Colors { get; }
70: }
71: ```
72: 
73: ### Grid Implementations
74: 
75: #### BrailleGrid
76: - **Resolution**: 2x4 dots per terminal cell
77: - **Storage**: UTF-16 code points for Braille patterns (0x2800-0x28FF)
78: - **Color Support**: Foreground only (no individual dot background colors)
79: - **Memory Efficiency**: Most compact representation for high-resolution drawing
80: 
81: #### HalfBlockGrid  
82: - **Resolution**: 1x2 pixels per terminal cell
83: - **Storage**: Color matrix with per-pixel color information
84: - **Color Support**: Full foreground and background control per terminal cell
85: - **Character Selection**: Space, upper half block (▀), lower half block (▄), full block (█)
86: 
87: #### CharGrid
88: - **Resolution**: 1x1 character per terminal cell  
89: - **Storage**: Character array with associated colors
90: - **Color Support**: Foreground color per cell
91: - **Character Selection**: Configurable character for drawing (dot, block, bar, etc.)
92: 
93: ### Coordinate System
94: 
95: ```csharp
96: public interface ICanvasPainter
97: {
98:     // Coordinate transformation
99:     (int X, int Y)? GetGridPoint(double canvasX, double canvasY);
100:     
101:     // Drawing operations
102:     void Paint(int gridX, int gridY, Color color);
103:     
104:     // Canvas properties
105:     (double[] XBounds, double[] YBounds) Bounds { get; }
106: }
107: ```
108: 
109: #### Coordinate Transformation Algorithm
110: ```csharp
111: public (int X, int Y)? GetGridPoint(double canvasX, double canvasY)
112: {
113:     var (left, right) = (XBounds[0], XBounds[1]);
114:     var (bottom, top) = (YBounds[0], YBounds[1]);
115:     
116:     // Check bounds
117:     if (canvasX < left || canvasX > right || canvasY < bottom || canvasY > top)
118:         return null;
119:         
120:     var width = right - left;
121:     var height = top - bottom;
122:     
123:     if (width <= 0.0 || height <= 0.0)
124:         return null;
125:     
126:     // Transform to grid coordinates (origin top-left)
127:     var gridX = (int)Math.Round((canvasX - left) * (Resolution.Width - 1) / width);
128:     var gridY = (int)Math.Round((top - canvasY) * (Resolution.Height - 1) / height);
129:     
130:     return (gridX, gridY);
131: }
132: ```
133: 
134: ### Shape Drawing Interface
135: 
136: The Canvas system must support drawing geometric shapes through a common interface:
137: 
138: ```csharp
139: public interface IShape
140: {
141:     void Draw(IPainter painter);
142: }
143: 
144: public interface IPainter
145: {
146:     void Paint(int x, int y, Color color);
147:     (int x, int y)? GetPoint(double worldX, double worldY);
148: }
149: ```
150: 
151: #### Circle Shape Implementation
152: 
153: ```csharp
154: public class Circle : IShape
155: {
156:     public double X { get; set; }           // Center X coordinate
157:     public double Y { get; set; }           // Center Y coordinate  
158:     public double Radius { get; set; }      // Circle radius
159:     public Color Color { get; set; }        // Circle color
160: 
161:     public Circle(double x, double y, double radius, Color color)
162:     {
163:         X = x;
164:         Y = y;
165:         Radius = radius;
166:         Color = color;
167:     }
168: 
169:     public void Draw(IPainter painter)
170:     {
171:         // Implementation details in WIDGET-CANVAS-CIRCLE-001 task
172:     }
173: }
174: ```
175: 
176: **Circle Rendering Requirements**:
177: - Must use parametric circle equation for point generation
178: - Should sample 360 points around circumference for smooth rendering
179: - Must handle coordinate transformation from world to screen coordinates
180: - Should gracefully handle points outside drawable area
181: - Must use high-precision floating-point operations where available
182: 
183: #### Points Shape Implementation
184: 
185: ```csharp
186: public class Points : IShape
187: {
188:     public IReadOnlyList<(double X, double Y)> Coordinates { get; set; }
189:     public Color Color { get; set; }
190: 
191:     public Points(IReadOnlyList<(double x, double y)> coordinates, Color color)
192:     {
193:         Coordinates = coordinates;
194:         Color = color;
195:     }
196: 
197:     public void Draw(IPainter painter)
198:     {
199:         foreach (var (x, y) in Coordinates)
200:         {
201:             if (painter.GetPoint(x, y) is var (gridX, gridY))
202:             {
203:                 painter.Paint(gridX, gridY, Color);
204:             }
205:         }
206:     }
207: }
208: ```
209: 
210: **Points Rendering Requirements**:
211: - Must efficiently process collections of coordinate tuples
212: - Should use readonly collections for memory efficiency
213: - Must apply single color to all points in collection
214: - Should use coordinate transformation for each point
215: - Must gracefully handle out-of-bounds coordinates via painter filtering
216: - Should optimize for large point collections where possible
217: - Must preserve floating-point precision during coordinate processing
218: 
219: ```csharp
220: public interface IShape
221: {
222:     void Draw(ICanvasPainter painter);
223: }
224: 
225: // Example shape implementations
226: public class Line : IShape
227: {
228:     public double X1 { get; set; }
229:     public double Y1 { get; set; }
230:     public double X2 { get; set; }
231:     public double Y2 { get; set; }
232:     public Color Color { get; set; }
233:     
234:     public void Draw(ICanvasPainter painter) { /* Bresenham line algorithm */ }
235: }
236: 
237: public class Rectangle : IShape
238: {
239:     public double X { get; set; }        // X position (bottom-left corner)
240:     public double Y { get; set; }        // Y position (bottom-left corner)
241:     public double Width { get; set; }    // Rectangle width
242:     public double Height { get; set; }   // Rectangle height
243:     public Color Color { get; set; }     // Rectangle border color
244:     
245:     public Rectangle(double x, double y, double width, double height, Color color)
246:     {
247:         X = x;
248:         Y = y;
249:         Width = width;
250:         Height = height;
251:         Color = color;
252:     }
253:     
254:     public void Draw(ICanvasPainter painter)
255:     {
256:         // Decompose rectangle into 4 line segments
257:         var lines = new[]
258:         {
259:             new Line(X, Y, X, Y + Height, Color),                    // Left edge
260:             new Line(X, Y + Height, X + Width, Y + Height, Color),   // Top edge  
261:             new Line(X + Width, Y, X + Width, Y + Height, Color),    // Right edge
262:             new Line(X, Y, X + Width, Y, Color)                      // Bottom edge
263:         };
264:         
265:         foreach (var line in lines)
266:         {
267:             line.Draw(painter);
268:         }
269:     }
270: }
271: 
272: public class Map : IShape
273: {
274:     public MapResolution Resolution { get; set; }
275:     public Color Color { get; set; }
276:     
277:     public void Draw(ICanvasPainter painter) { /* Map coordinate rendering */ }
278: }
279: 
280: public enum MapResolution
281: {
282:     Low,    // ~1000 coordinate points
283:     High    // ~5000 coordinate points  
284: }
285: ```
286: 
287: **Map Shape Requirements**:
288: - Must support two resolution levels with different point densities
289: - Should use pre-computed world coordinate data arrays
290: - Must integrate with canvas coordinate transformation system
291: - Should handle coordinate points outside drawable area gracefully
292: - Must support color customization through standard Color enum
293: - Should optimize for performance with large coordinate datasets
294: ```
